        "status": "connected_with_authority_limitations",
        "description": "USPA/IPSC \u2014 Use the American Target Company USPA/IPSC paper target for competition practice, using its printed face as the aiming reference. Session instructions and applicable rules must be independently governed. Artwork-review evidence describes: Single light outlined geometric torso silhouette with a narrow rectangular head tab, angular shoulders and chamfered lower corners; no visible printed score numbers. Present the exact USPA/IPSC target identity and captured shot evidence. Explain the visible layout without treating illustrations, printed markings, or pixel positions as verified Backend scoring regions. Shooter feedback may describe observations, but must not claim an authoritative zone, point value, or qualification result absent governed boundaries and rules. EVIDENCE ONLY under the current contracts. Do not award points, certify qualification, issue numeric sight corrections, or assign authoritative hit/miss regions without separately verified publisher/session rules and physical Backend geometry. Do not double-count shots. Pixels are representation, never Backend authority.",
